
## --help
rc=0
git.grove.auth.github.set — put a github token on a grove's rack, securely

usage:
  rhx git.grove.auth.github.set <grove> [--mode plan|apply] [--refresh]

options:
  --mode     plan (default) or apply
  --refresh  re-set a slug that already answers (rotated or expired pat)
  --env      keyrack env; default camp
  --owner    keyrack owner; default ehmpath
  --org      org sigil for the slug; default @all (every org reads it)

a camp grove only: on a local or house grove the token lives in os.secure, set on the box.

the value is TYPED on the box over an interactive ssh tty — never passed
as an argument, never sent down a duct. see the header for why.

## a local or house grove → refused at rung 0b
rc=2
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; a camp grove's identity answers it)
   └─ drive
      ├─ box  reachable at 'grove-x'
      └─ ✋ ConstraintError: grove 'grove-x' is not a camp grove (its GROVE_ENV_SERVER is local@unix)

  why: this skill stores the token in aws.params, and only a camp grove holds
       the camp identity that reads it back. a local or house grove would get
       a value written into whatever account its shell holds
  fix: keep the token in os.secure instead — run this ON that grove, at a tty:
    cd ~/git/more/dev-env-setup && rhx keyrack set \
      --owner ehmpath --key GITHUB_TOKEN --org @all --env camp --vault os.secure
    (or, on a box with a human: gh auth login)

## a camp grove with no live identity → refused at rung 0b
rc=2
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; a camp grove's identity answers it)
   └─ drive
      ├─ box  reachable at 'grove-x'
      └─ ✋ ConstraintError: grove 'grove-x' is a camp grove, and its camp identity does not answer

  why: a camp grove carries the camp aws identity by MANDATE, on every seat;
       this seat's [default] chain answered no identity, so aws.params is
       unreadable here and a set would be read back by naught
  fix: on hetzner, infra wires [default] to its IAM Roles Anywhere signer —
       run ahbode/infrastructure's grove identity skill for this seat; on ec2,
       the instance role is detached. then prove it on the box:
    rhx git.grove.send grove-x --what 'rhx grove.provision --what 5.6.aws --mode apply'

## a box with no checkout → rc 1, never read as not-camp
rc=1
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; a camp grove's identity answers it)
   └─ drive
      ├─ box  reachable at 'grove-x'
      └─ 💥 MalfunctionError: grove 'grove-x' could not name its own tier

  why: its derive did not answer — no checkout at ~/git/more/dev-env-setup/src, or a derive
       that fails closed (a hetzner box with no /etc/grove/platform yet)
  it said:
    bash: line 1: /home/<seat>/git/more/dev-env-setup/src/grove.env.sh: No such file or directory
  fix: provision it first — the boot lays the checkout and the platform:
    rhx git.grove.provision boot grove-x --mode apply

## the control · a camp grove → passes rung 0b, plan only
rc=0
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; a camp grove's identity answers it)
   └─ drive
      ├─ box  reachable at 'grove-x'
      ├─ camp the box is a camp grove and its identity answers, so aws.params is readable
      ├─ rhx  present
      ├─ rhx  runs (keyrack answered)
      └─ ✔ the rack already answers for GITHUB_TOKEN — no work

🔑 already set!
   ├─ to replace a rotated or expired pat: --refresh
   └─ to prove gh accepts it:
      rhx git.grove.send grove-x --what 'gh auth status'

## a camp grove, the slug absent → the plan, rc 0
rc=0
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; a camp grove's identity answers it)
   └─ drive
      ├─ box  reachable at 'grove-x'
      ├─ camp the box is a camp grove and its identity answers, so aws.params is readable
      ├─ rhx  present
      ├─ rhx  runs (keyrack answered)
      ├─ rack does NOT answer for GITHUB_TOKEN — a human is owed
      └─ plan — this is what apply would run ON THE BOX:

         cd ~/git/more/dev-env-setup
         rhx keyrack set  --owner ehmpath --key GITHUB_TOKEN \
                          --org @all --env camp --vault aws.params

      the set PROMPTS twice on the box's own tty — mechanism (answer 1),
      then the token. mint it at https://github.com/settings/tokens with
      scopes: repo, read:org

      ⚠️ one set, and no 'keyrack fill' after it. set stores the value
         itself; fill re-drives those same two prompts, so a chained fill
         takes the pat as its MECHANISM answer and keyrack rejects it with
         expected: "1-2"

      re-run with --mode apply to be handed that prompt.

## a probe that hangs → ended by the bound, rc 1 (a malfunction)
rc=1
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; a camp grove's identity answers it)
   └─ drive
      ├─ box  reachable at 'grove-x'
      └─ 💥 MalfunctionError: grove 'grove-x' did not answer the tier probe within 2s

  why: a login shell on the box held the session past the bound — an rc line
       that waits, or a derive with no answer. the tier is unknown, not denied
  fix: read the box's own derive, then re-run —
    rhx git.grove.send grove-x --what 'rhx grove.provision --mode plan'

## a grove that does not answer → rc 1, names the wake
rc=1
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; a camp grove's identity answers it)
   └─ drive
      └─ 💥 MalfunctionError: grove 'grove-x' does not answer at ssh alias 'grove-x'

  why: the box is asleep, or its tunnel is not bound
  fix: wake it — a wake is idempotent
    rhx git.grove.wake grove-x

